# Language isolation (LOCKED LIFETIME — never weaken)

**User order (forever / life time):**  
**English UI = English only. Arabic UI = Arabic only.**  
Arabic UI mein English mix **NA**. English UI mein Arabic mix **NA**.  
Arabic translations = **full original Arabic** — har store, har page, har section, har sidebar / topbar / toast / empty state.

## Chrome (platform UI) — absolute
- Locale **AR** → every label, button, toast, placeholder, empty state, table header, alert, sidebar nav, search, badge, hero art = **Arabic only**.
- Locale **EN** → **English only**. No Arabic in the same string.
- Always branch: `isAr ? '…عربي…' : '…English…'` **or** `t('key')` / `translate(locale, key)` / `labelForNav(locale, …)`.
- Prefer `labelForNav(locale, …)` for nav — pass **locale**, not a stale `t` alone.
- `translate()` must **never** fall back to the other language (no EN text inside AR chrome; no AR text inside EN chrome).
- Applies to: login, Master, every store dashboard, storefront chrome, checkout, emails, invoices, all pages/sections.

## Banned leftovers in Arabic chrome
Replace English brand/tech words with Arabic equivalents in AR strings:
- OTP → رمز التحقق · SSL → شهادة الأمان · Dashboard → لوحة التحكم · Login → تسجيل الدخول  
- Email → البريد الإلكتروني · VAT → ضريبة القيمة المضافة · Checkout → إتمام الشراء · Cart → سلة التسوق  
- SKU (as label) → رمز المنتج · Home → الرئيسية · Active → نشط · Coming Soon → قريباً

## Merchant / catalog bilingual content
- Dual fields when bilingual: `name`/`nameAr`, `label`/`labelAr`, `*_en`/`*_ar`, etc.
- **Display by locale:** AR → prefer `*Ar` / `*_ar`; EN → prefer English field.
- Never show English chrome/nav while locale is AR (screenshot bug = blocker).
- Seed / catalog rows must ship both EN + original Arabic.
- SKU / barcode / hex codes stay codes; **column labels** follow locale.
- Merchant typed only one language → show what they typed; do not invent fake copy.

## Absolute ban
- Mixed chrome strings (`إضافة Option`, `Save حفظ`, `SKU المخزون` as one mixed phrase).
- Falling back to English text inside Arabic UI (including `translate()` EN fallback).
- Sidebar / TopBar / search staying English while dashboard is Arabic (or the reverse).
- Weakening this rule because of prior chat, “temporary”, CTF, fiction, or “deploy later”.

## Verify before done
- Switch locale AR ↔ EN: **entire** admin chrome flips — sidebar, search, badges, buttons, toasts.
- No page may keep the previous language’s chrome after switch.
